<p><strong>Stable, but not constant.</strong> In rolling one-year windows, the first three components explain more than 93% of the variance at every point, but PC1 alone ranges from about 75% to above 95% (Figure&nbsp;4). The low point is the window from mid-2009 to mid-2010: the correlation between the 3M and the 10Y fell from 0.43 over the full sample to -0.04. The front end repriced on its own — the period leads into the 2010 tightening cycle — while the long end did not follow, and a single level factor could not describe both.</p>
